{
    "background_story": "Carson was a brilliant architect with a fascination for geometry and spatial reasoning. As a child, he spent hours playing with Rubik's Cube, mastering the art of solving it in record time. This early passion led him to design innovative buildings that defied conventional shapes. His magnum opus was the 'Cube Complex', a futuristic skyscraper composed of interconnected cubes that seemed to float in mid-air. The structure became an instant landmark, attracting visitors from around the world. Carson's love for the cube extended beyond architecture; he believed that its symmetry and balance held secrets to a more harmonious and efficient world. His work inspired a new generation of designers to think outside the box \u2013 or in this case, inside the cube.",
